  "question": {
    "text": "There is a crater of depth <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mi>R</mi> <mrow> <mn>100</mn></mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> on the surface of the moon, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the radius of the moon. A ball is projected vertically upwards from the crater with a velocity which is equal to the escape velocity from the surface of the moon. If the maximum height attained by the particle is close to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is an integer, then find the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "99",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Speed of particle at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>At point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>By conservation of energy,</p><p>decrease in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KE</mi><mo>=</mo></math> increase in GPE</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mi>Mv</mi><mi>Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>·</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>GM</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>99</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>·</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>98</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>98</mn><mo>]</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>98</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>99</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p>"
